# ── The agent toolchain: present on this machine, never committed ──────────────
# The split is by AUDIENCE, not by tool.
#
# AGENTS.md is VERSIONED and public: it is the cross-vendor contract for the code
# itself — the layer arrow, the format registry, the red zone, the testing rule and
# the traps already paid for. Anyone who clones this repository, human or agent,
# needs it, and it depends on no tool being installed.
#
# Everything below is about THIS MACHINE's setup rather than about the code: which
# agents are reachable, which models, which skills exist, how delegation works.
# It would be noise in a public repository and it goes stale the moment someone
# else clones it.
#
# The agent-specific file imports AGENTS.md and holds only the machine-specific half.
.claude/
.crew/
CLAUDE.md
START.md
.mcp.json
.mcp.json.example
.crew-kit-config
.crew-kit-config.example

# .github/ is NOT ignored — the PR template stays with the repository.

# ── Go ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The build output. Added because `go build -o imgconv` drops it right here and a
# committed binary is noise; delete this line if you ever want to ship one.
/imgconv
/imgconv.exe

# The release build output. scripts/build-release.sh writes here.
/dist/

# Test binaries and coverage
*.test
*.out
